      "id": "gh_0da1549c7daf4a0c09a7d121",
      "sourceId": "jobright-ai/2026-Software-Engineer-New-Grad#9",
      "title": "[Product Bug] Jobs auto-detected as \"Applied\" remain visible in \"Liked\" tab (cross-tab duplication)",
      "description": "Hi Jobright team. Filing here because this repo is the most public-visible surface; please route to the extension / web-app product team.\n\n### Bug\n\nAfter the Chrome extension auto-detects a submitted application, the job stays in **both** the \"Liked\" tab AND the \"Applied\" tab. User has to manually un-Like each one or Liked-tab counts inflate indefinitely.\n\n### Repro\n\n1. Save a job to the Liked list (click heart/save on a job card)\n2. Apply to that same job on the external careers page\n3. Return to Jobright dashboard\n4. Observe: job appears in both Applied AND Liked\n\n### Expected\n\nOnce auto-detect flips a job to Applied, it should disappear from Liked. \"Applied\" supersedes \"Liked\" in the user's pipeline model: you don't \"like\" a job you've already committed to.\n\n### Impact\n\nBreaks pipeline tracking integrity. Any user with 20+ liked jobs who applies to a few per day accumulates a growing phantom Liked list that no longer reflects pipeline state. Appears to be a recurring class of complaint in third-party Jobright reviews (weak submission tracking).\n\n### One-click diagnostic for your eng team\n\nHard-refresh the Liked tab after reproducing:\n\n- **Duplicate persists**: backend data model issue (likely independent `isLiked` + `isApplied` boolean flags with no mutex, or separate collections with no cross-delete on apply-event)\n- **Duplicate clears**: frontend cache-invalidation miss on apply-event (likely Chrome extension writes applied status without invalidating the Liked-list query)\n\n### Fix sketch\n\n- **Write-side**: on apply-event, set `isLiked=false` as well, OR migrate to a single `status` enum (liked / applied / interviewing / rejected) that is mutually exclusive\n- **Query-side (belt-and-suspenders)**: filter Liked by `isLiked AND status != 'applied' AND status != 'interviewing'` so the bug cannot recur via other write paths\n\n### Severity\n\n**High**. Not critical (no data loss, no security issue), but breaks the extension's core value prop of trustworthy pipeline tracking. 200K users times this friction = material NPS impact.\n\nHappy to provide screenshots if that unblocks routing.",
      "excerpt": "Hi Jobright team. Filing here because this repo is the most public-visible surface; please route to the extension / web-app product team. ### Bug After the Chrome extension auto-detects a submitted application, the jo...",
